parts.text:
Good news:
- Episode rows ALREADY have download icons (lines 404-413) calling `handleDownload(ep)`. But `startDownload` only saves a metadata record to localStorage — it does NOT save the actual video file to local disk. The user wants "episode is downloaded to local files" — an actual file download.

**Upgrade startDownload to a REAL download**: fetch the video URL as blob → createObjectURL → anchor click with `download` attribute → browser saves to local Downloads folder. Also keep the in-app record. Handle CORS: fetching cross-origin videos may fail CORS; fallback: direct anchor navigation to URL (browser may still download if Content-Disposition, else opens). Best-effort:

```ts
const startDownload = async (media, episode?) => {
  // premium gate...
  const url = episode ? episode.videoUrl : media.videoUrl;
  const fileName = ...;
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url); // may fail CORS
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error();
    const blob = await res.blob();
    const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    triggerAnchor(objectUrl, fileName);
    setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(objectUrl), 60000);
  } catch {
    // CORS fallback: open in new tab / direct href
    const a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = url; a.download = fileName; a.target = '_blank'; a.rel='noopener';
    document.body.appendChild(a); a.click(); a.remove();
  }
  // record in downloads list
}
```

Note: for YouTube/embed URLs blob fetch makes no sense — fallback anchor handles it (opens tab). Fine.

Also show per-episode downloading state (spinner) — handleDownload already sets downloadingId and clears after 1.2s. With real fetch it could take longer; make startDownload awaited inside handleDownload and clear state on completion. Update MovieDetailsModal handleDownload to await properly:

```ts
const handleDownload = async (episode?: Episode) => {
  const idKey = episode ? episode.id : media.id;
  setDownloadingId(idKey);
  await startDownload(media, episode);
  setDownloadingId(null);
};
```
And button shows RotateCw spinner when downloadingId === ep.id, plus check icon when downloaded? Keep simple: spinner while active.

**Feature 1: Watch Now auto-plays E01 of Season 1.**
Update currentEpisodes + Watch Now:
```ts
// merged episodes sorted by season/number
const allEpisodes = [...(media.episodes||[]), ...(media.seasons||[]).flatMap(s=>(s.episodes||[]).map(ep=>({...ep, season: ep.season || s.seasonNumber})))]
  .sort((a,b)=>(a.season-b.season)||(a.episodeNumber-b.episodeNumber));
const firstEpisode = allEpisodes[0];
```
Watch Now onClick: `startPlayback(media, firstEpisode)`.

Also episodes section condition uses `media.episodes && length>0` — use allEpisodes instead so seasons-only series show episodes too. And currentEpisodes should filter from allEpisodes by selectedSeason.

Season switcher builds buttons from `media.seasonsCount || 1` — better to derive from actual seasons present in allEpisodes. Improve: unique seasons from allEpisodes.

**Feature 2 already works** (5s countdown → auto-start next without action). But improve sequencing correctness: sort episodesList in VideoPlayer by season+episodeNumber so "next" is correct across seasons. Also when last episode of season ends and next season exists, hasNextEpisode logic covers via merged list ✓ after sorting.

Also make sure VideoPlayer episodesList sorted:
```ts
return [...merged].sort((a,b)=>((a.season||1)-(b.season||1))||((a.episodeNumber||0)-(b.episodeNumber||0)));
```

Also "if user opens season episode01 is played automatically": additionally, clicking a SEASON TAB in details modal → maybe play first ep of that season? That'd be surprising UX; skip. Watch Now = S01E01 ✓.

DownloadsPage shows saved items with playable videoUrl — fine.

Implement now:
1. AppContext.startDownload real file download.
2. MovieDetailsModal: merged/sorted episodes, firstEpisode autoplay on Watch Now, episodes UI from merged list, season tabs derived from data, await download state, spinner icon.
3. VideoPlayer: sort episodesList.
Then build+restart+verify.

